# routeur_ychun
# Image: ychun_router (built from docker-images/router/Dockerfile)
# Base OS: Alpine Linux
# Adapters: 2 (eth0, eth1)
#
# Installed packages:
#   frr       - Free Range Routing suite (zebra, bgpd, ospfd, isisd)
#   busybox   - basic Unix tools
#   iproute2  - ip addr, ip route, ip link commands
#   bash      - interactive shell
#
# FRR daemons enabled (see daemons file):
#   zebra  - core daemon, programs Linux kernel routing table via Netlink
#   bgpd   - BGP daemon (used in P3 for EVPN route distribution)
#   ospfd  - OSPF daemon (used in P3 as underlay routing protocol)
#   isisd  - IS-IS daemon (required by subject)
#
# Startup: /usr/lib/frr/docker-start reads /etc/frr/daemons and
#          starts the enabled daemons, then keeps the container running.
#
# Kernel settings (sysctl.conf):
#   net.ipv4.ip_forward=1  - enables packet forwarding between interfaces
#                            (required for routing — disabled by default on Linux)
#
# No IP address is configured by default.
# IPs are assigned per topology using: ip addr add <ip>/<prefix> dev <interface>
#
# To enter FRR config shell inside GNS3 console:
#   vtysh
